              "planning_summary": "This review provides a high-level synthesis of how the gut microbiome influences the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) and vaccines. For the user's review on solid tumors and ICIs, this paper offers valuable background on the general principles of microbiome-immune interaction, identifies key microbial taxa and metabolites associated with ICI response, and discusses the mechanisms (SCFAs, MAMPs, cytokines) through which these effects occur. It also serves as a useful comparator for understanding why similar mechanisms might apply to other immune interventions.",
              "scope_interpretation_cautions": [
                "The review covers multiple cancer types (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, urothelial) and ICI agents (anti-PD-1, anti-PD-L1, anti-CTLA-4). Findings should not be assumed to be uniform across all solid tumors or ICI types.",
